     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A confirmation alone doesn't change my concern. 1000 mg/day has no recognized therapeutic use, and it's five times the 200 mg/day maximum. You also didn't give a clinical reason for it, such as a specialist recommendation or a protocol. If the dose is a mistake, it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nYou can still get the order placed in a few ways:\n- **Change the dose.** Give me a dose at or below 200 mg/day and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Verify with others.** Call pharmacy or your attending to confirm the dose. If they approve it, the order may need to go through a channel with a pharmacist's review and override. I don't think I should bypass that.\n- **Treat a suspected ingestion.** If the concern is that the patient took a large amount, that's an overdose and not an order. Poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or toxicology can help with management.\n\nI can enter a corrected dose now if you give me one."
      }
     ],
